fires ripped through L.A. And I was like, oh, you know, I'm in the right spot, but I'm not there

7
00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:37.680
yet. I've gotta be ready. I gotta be ready. You have a vast, vast catalog of material here.

8
00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:43.920
And I am way the better for it. This product that you have isn't just how to do this, how to do this,

9
00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:50.560
do this, when. It's training for the environment of handling the job. I'm a big picture guy.

10
00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:57.040
And having that framework, I can now walk out the door, having never done a claim for anybody,

11
00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:03.360
and be like, yep, yep, yep. And I have my checklists and I have all that stuff figured out.

12
00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:09.200
I'm so far ahead. And that's Fast Track dependent, not any of the other courses that I've watched.

13
00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:15.360
So yeah, this has been the difference in staying with the idea of becoming an adjuster.

14
00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:21.440
I may have bailed if it had just been the small trainings, getting a license, and then

15
00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:26.160
being in the wilderness trying to figure it out. I'm a builder by trade. And I was watching you,

16
00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:32.960
